  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Give four unique spellings of one consonant-l-e word. One is the real spelling.",
      "Never put the target word in the stem. Use a short kid-world clue. Add a lemma picture when the word is a concrete noun.",
      "Tier 1 distractors drop a letter or swap le to el in a loud way.",
      "Tier 2 distractors stay grade-level: le versus el, missing final e, or a wrong vowel in the first syllable.",
      "Tier 3 distractors are near-misses: el for le, a dropped double consonant, or a real-looking wrong vowel.",
      "Use kid-world CLe words from home, food, pets, play, school, family, or weather. No brands. No real names.",
      "Every choice is a whole word. Never IPA, never a lone sound, never a letter name as the answer.",
      "Shuffle the correct index. Do not always put the right spelling first."
    ]
  },
